      "name": "Mo-Si-B alloy",
      "material_category": "refractory intermetallic alloy",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": 14,
          "section": "1.1 Introduction",
          "quote": "The intermetallic alloys based on the Mo-Si-B system have been chosen for study in this research program",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "e3f8552003a8f958:part:001"
        },
        {
          "page": 22,
          "section": "2.3 Oxidation Behavior",
          "quote": "Studies of the oxidation mechanisms of the ơ-Mo+Mo3Si+T2 system have established that the enhanced oxidation resistance is provided by the formations of a continuous, stable, protective borosilicate glass layer at temperatures between 1000-1300°C, which retards the volatilization of the ơ-Mo phase [10].",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "e3f8552003a8f958:part:002"
        },
        {
          "page": 27,
          "section": "2.4 Mechanical Properties",
          "quote": "The previous research work clearly approved that significant flexibility exists in the multiphase Mo-Si-B alloy system for controlling microstructure through novel processing, chemistry modification, phase transformation, which results in the desired mechanical properties. Therefore, the system is collectively made as a representative of the next generation of ultra high temperature alloys for structural applications.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "e3f8552003a8f958:part:002"
        },
        {
          "page": "70",
          "section": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "quote": "The main conclusions arising from this project on the high temperature compression creep behavior of Mo-Si-B alloys are outlined below.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "e3f8552003a8f958:part:003"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
